# Memli Stack

- App lives under `dev/memli/`.
  - `apps/web`: Vite + React frontend (`TanStack Router`).
  - `packages/core` (`@workspace/core`): Pure TypeScript domain logic (SuperMemo SM-2 `gradeCard()`, zero React/DOM imports).
  - `packages/schemas` (`@workspace/schemas`): Shared Zod validation contracts and environment schemas.
  - `packages/ui` (`@workspace/ui`): Web-only component library built on shadcn/ui + Base UI primitives, including reusable `<Section>`, `<Heading>`, and `<Text>` layout/typography primitives.
- Routing: **TanStack Router** (`Link`, `createFileRoute`, file routes under `apps/web/src/routes`).
- Styling: **Tailwind CSS** + `cn()` from `@workspace/ui/lib/utils`.
- Components: **shadcn/ui** (Base UI primitives). Import from `@workspace/ui/components/*`.
- Icons: **lucide-react**.
- Button composition: use `render={<Link ... />}` and `nativeButton={false}` — not `asChild` (this is Base UI, not Radix).

## Brand

- Product name today: **Memli** (planned public rebrand: **FluentVine** — coordinate renames in a branding pass).
- Desktop logo: BookOpen icon in a primary-colored rounded square + "Memli" text.
- Prefer semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) over hard-coded blues.

## Product & architecture docs

- Long-lived decisions: `docs/` (start at `docs/roadmap.md`).
- Always-on UX / i18n / architecture / state constraints: `product-ux.mdc`, `i18n-foundations.mdc`, `architecture-guardrails.mdc`, `react-state.mdc`.

## State

- Follow `react-state.mdc`: server data → TanStack Query, URL-worthy → Router search params, lifecycle/coupled → `useReducer` + discriminated union (pure transitions in `packages/core`), `useState` only for one uncoupled primitive.
- Enforced by `memli/no-use-state-sprawl` (max one `useState` per component in `apps/web`, outside `_marketing` / `_auth`).

## Prefer composition over new packages

- Check existing shadcn components before adding.
- A single open/close toggle is the one `useState` case; do not add libraries for one toggle. Two or more related values are a reducer, not a library.

